# Research ODE invariants

- NEVER modify `hybrid_loss()` masking or `color_mask` handling
  (`ode/training_loop.py`, the physiology block that gates Z). Masked Z
  frames are already excluded from `phys_loss`; `val_mse_Z` is computed
  only on valid frames.
- NEVER reintroduce xy centroid loss. `xy_loss_weight` stays `0.0`.
- NEVER change affine decoder init, freeze schedule, or scale math.
  `output_scale` / `output_bias` start frozen.
- Default trainer dynamics are `StableSigmoidalODEFunc`
  (`dz/dt = rate · σ(sat − z)`). `--ode-type sigmoidal` is the legacy
  Verhulst form `r · z · (1 − z/K)` with positive SiLU/softplus heads.
  Step 8 Zwietering–Richards (`--rhs zwietering`) is an explicit request.
  Do not swap the default without an explicit request.
- After ANY training change, report: `train_dz_dt_size_std`,
  `z_traj/acceleration_ratio`, `val_track_mse_mean`, per-track r/K
  (or μ/λ/ν) variance.
- Keep `ode_nfe` under 60.
- `normalize_z0` stays ON permanently. Ablation a/a+b collapsed
  z0 norms to ~0.09; do not pass `--no-normalize-z0`.
- Track embeddings are an H1 (known-track) symmetry breaker only.
  They do not solve encoder identifiability (z0 cosine ~0.996) for H2.
- Reproducibility: every job logs `git_hash` + dirty flag. The trainer
  refuses to start on a missing repo or dirty tree unless `--allow-dirty`.
- `checkpoints/h1_final_best/` is read-only. Do not retrain, overwrite,
  or write any file under that directory. It is a leaked 80/20 historical
  artifact (D-009). Identity is SHA256
  `2498d033ea02e2df1e312a58179226b649a9d3d5c7143b2d040fc9341ef86222`.
  Exclude it from all H1 means going forward.
- K-in-window is unidentifiable on this data (NLS K ~279 px vs latent
  bound 2). Size carrying capacity stays out of window (K=10 latent)
  unless explicitly requested otherwise.
- Lag is a Zwietering parameter λ, not a multiplicative gate.
